			"Message": "feat(Mountain/Environment): Implement output channel management trait\n\nIntroduces `OutputProvider.rs` implementing `OutputChannelManager` trait for `MountainEnvironment`, enabling core output channel operations required for extension and UI interactions. This:\n\n- Provides concrete implementation for channel lifecycle management (register/append/clear/reveal/dispose) through `Handlers::Output` effect logic\n- Integrates with Mountain's async effect system using `async_trait` for Tauri-compatible async operations\n- Adds structured logging for output channel operations to support debugging\n- Implements `Requires` trait binding for dependency injection in Mountain's runtime\n\nThis fulfills part of MVP Deliverable #5 (Basic Extension Support) by enabling extension-side output channels to communicate with Mountain's backend through the `Track` dispatcher and `Echo` API contract. The implementation follows Mountain's handler pattern seen in recent document provider work (ref a96dc09).",
