			"Message": "feat(AppState): Add terminal instance state management\n\nIntroduce `TerminalState` struct in Mountain's AppState to represent active terminal sessions. This structure:\n- Captures shell configuration (path, args, cwd, env variables)\n- Tracks OS process identifiers and PTY status\n- Manages async communication channels (PtyInputTransmitter)\n- Handles task lifecycle via Tokio JoinHandles for output reading and process waiting\n\nSupports MVP deliverable #5 (basic extension support) by providing necessary state infrastructure for terminal operations initiated through Cocoon extensions. The design aligns with Land's architecture by:\n1. Using Tokio primitives for async process management\n2. Leveraging serde for potential serialization\n3. Integrating with Mountain's AppState system\n4. Preparing for future ProcessMgmt integration in Runner component\n\nEnables future terminal features while maintaining VS Code compatibility through option parsing from extension-provided JSON values.",
