			"Message": "chore(Vine): Add legacy message structures for stdio IPC compatibility\n\nIntroduces VineMessage and VineMessageType enums to maintain backwards compatibility with the legacy stdio-based IPC protocol during transition to gRPC. These structures:\n- Mirror historical JSON message format used by Cocoon sidecar\n- Support deserialization of existing IPC traffic\n- Include serde aliases for field name variations\n\nThis transitional implementation allows Mountain to handle both legacy Vine IPC and new gRPC communication channels simultaneously, ensuring uninterrupted operation during the protocol migration phase of MVP Path A. The commented deprecation notice clarifies the eventual replacement by proto-defined gRPC messages from recent commits (98f5b90, 8704966).\n\nMaintains compatibility with current Cocoon shims while progressing towards more efficient RPC mechanisms outlined in Land's architecture.",
